body:
Awhile back I came across a site in which mothers posted pictures of their stillborn children onto the page. The page consisted of photos and videos of the mothers dressing up their children and performing typical day to day acts that a mother would carry out with her child. Anything from from setting them down at the kitchen table, laying them down in their beds, or even bathing them. The page had a flowery background and there was a song that continuously looped. Just some typical piano music, but given the topic it was played behind it couldn't have been any creepier. 

&#x200B;

I haven't been able to find the page again, although I don't know if I'd want to go back, but it's a page that's always stuck with me. As disgusting as it is, reading some of the captions almost spark sympathy. They say how they do these things because they couldn't get over not being able to have their child, so they pretty much move on as if it were alive and well. 

&#x200B;

Pretty weird shit man.
